This is my angelic sister Marie. You may use one syllable of her name. Thus, I dub you

37
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:06,280
97

38
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:08,280
The birdie's tough. He needs a cooler name than that

39
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:10,280
Let me think for a sec

40
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:14,280
Call him Magnum Fire

41
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:15,280
That's lame

42
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:18,280
Seriously, you've got the worst taste ever

43
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:20,280
No, that would be you

44
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:21,280
I don't know

45
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:22,280
I don't know

46
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:23,280
I don't know

47
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:24,280
I don't know

48
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:25,280
I don't know

49
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:26,280
I don't know

50
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:27,280
I don't know

51
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:32,280
Mind if I fatten the bird up? I've got a craving for drumsticks and it looks tasty

52
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:34,280
Not a chance

53
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:36,280
You think it'll lay eggs?

54
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:37,280
Huh?

55
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:39,280
This guy's Birdie Boy

56
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:42,280
No, his name is Silvante Schnauzer

57
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:45,280
No, it's Birdie Boy

58
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:47,280
He likes Silvante Schnauzer better

59
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,280
Birdie Boy

60
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:51,280
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

61
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:53,280
Hey, what's that for, Birdie Boy?

62
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:55,280
See, I was right

63
00:05:57,280 --> 00:06:00,280
You prefer Silvante Schnauzer, don't you?

64
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:02,280
Huh? Huh?

65
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:04,280
He likes Magnum Fire!

66
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,280
Ma

67
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:06,280
No, wine

68
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:10,280
How about we name him Nero?

69
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:12,280
Next time

70
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:14,280
There, I think he likes it

71
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:16,280
It means black, cool, huh?

72
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:17,280
Nero

73
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:18,280
Uh

74
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:19,280
What the?

75
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:23,280
Okay

76
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:24,280
Listen up, guys

77
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:25,280
Yes

78
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:26,280
Yummy, sir

79
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:28,280
Hi, gang

80
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:29,280
How's it going?

81
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:31,280
Hey, welcome back

82
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:34,280
What did they want you to schlep over to the castle for?

83
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:38,280
Is it a mission? I really hope it's a mission

84
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:40,280
Then we can all go together

85
00:06:40,280 --> 00:06:41,280
Well, sir

86
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:42,280
Is it a mission?

87
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:44,280
Kinda

88
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:46,280
Pay attention, everyone hears what's going on

89
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:50,280
I was called in because they've discovered a new dungeon

90
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:54,280
A new dungeon? Seriously?

91
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:55,280
You mean it, Yummy, sir?

92
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:57,280
Wow!

93
00:06:57,280 --> 00:06:59,280
That's all I saw was a dungeon

94
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:00,280
Huh?

95
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:03,280
Dude, are you kidding me?

96
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:05,280
What are you acting shocked for when you don't even know what it is?

97
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:07,280
Everyone else was

98
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:08,280
Typical roster

99
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:09,280
Ugh

100
00:07:09,280 --> 00:07:11,280
Listen up, Dungeons 101

101
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:16,280
Dungeons are like tombs where people from way back store their most valuable stuff

102
00:07:16,280 --> 00:07:19,280
Sometimes they've got powerful ancient magic techniques

103
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:21,280
Or sweet magic items inside

104
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:24,280
What I'm saying is dungeons totally rock!

105
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:26,280
One thing, though

106
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,280
Hmm?

107
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:28,280
They kinda try to kill you

108
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:34,280
The folks who build them added all sorts of crazy trap spells to keep people from getting to their stuff and misusing it

109
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:38,280
So they're seriously dangerous and seriously fun, too

110
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:44,280
Exploring a dungeon's kinda like going on a treasure hunt where you could die at any second

111
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:47,280
You can see why it's the sort of thing they only leave to magic nights

112
00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:49,280
Yeah, sure

113
00:07:49,280 --> 00:07:51,280
So, a new dungeon showed up

114
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:53,280
And then Captain Yomi was called to the castle

115
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:56,280
I'm guessing that means the Black Bulls are being sent to explore it

116
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:57,280
That's right

117
00:07:57,280 --> 00:08:00,280
And it's in a dicey location

118
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:03,280
Popped up near our border with an enemy country

119
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:04,280
An enemy?

120
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:06,280
Yeah, the Diamond Kanon

121
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:10,280
This mission has to be carried out swiftly and thoroughly

122
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:13,280
We want to keep those diamond guys' paws off the good stuff

123
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:15,280
Who knows what could happen?

124
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:20,280
In the past, people have found items in dungeons that could change civilization itself

125
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:23,280
Some explorers have even come out of them able to use the most powerful magic-

126
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:26,280
Oh! Oh! Send me! Please send me, Captain Yomi, sir!

127
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:29,280
Maybe I'll be able to learn how to use the most powerful magic

128
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:32,280
Yeah? How you gonna do that without any magic?

129
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:35,280
It could work! I won't know until I try!

130
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:39,280
Magic power or not, you are going on this mission, kid

131
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:41,280
Wasn't my call this time, so don't look at me

132
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:43,280
The Wizard King asked for you

133
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:44,280
What?

134
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:46,280
WHAT?!

135
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:49,280
The Wizard King?! There's no way!

136
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:52,280
Hey, that's awesome, Oscar! Good for you!

137
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:55,280
So, what's the deal? You got an in with the Wizard King or something?

138
00:08:55,280 --> 00:08:58,280
No! Not at all!

139
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:01,280
The Wizard King actually chose me!

140
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:03,280
I don't know why, but...

141
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:04,280
Oh, wow!

142
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:06,280
Wizard King, sir!

143
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:08,280
I've got this!

144
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:09,280
Count on me!

145
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:12,280
I will devote myself to this mission, body and soul!

146
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:15,280
Well, that's one! Noelle, you should go too!

147
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:16,280
Uh...

148
00:09:16,280 --> 00:09:18,280
It's all about getting experience, isn't it?

149
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:20,280
And last but not least is luck!

150
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:21,280
Hm?

151
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:23,280
I want you to take the lead on this one!

152
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:25,280
The newbies are all yours!

153
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:26,280
Uh...

154
00:09:26,280 --> 00:09:27,280
Really? Me?

155
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:30,280
Sure! You're gonna lose your edge if you're always here holding down the fort!

156
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:31,280
Thank you, sir!

157
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:36,280
And less than luck! The rookies are your responsibilities, so look after them!

158
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:37,280
Yeah! Don't worry!

159
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:43,280
I wanna go too! It makes me sad to be left behind!

160
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:45,280
Sure!

161
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:50,280
Be careful out there!

162
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:52,280
Do your best, you two!

163
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:53,280
Go give them hell!

164
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:54,280
Yes, sir!

165
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:55,280
I suppose we can do that.

166
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:59,280
I wonder how many ladies I can pick up while you three are exploring the dungeon.

167
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:00,280
Hm?

168
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:01,280
Huh?

169
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:03,280
Since I'm not needed, may I visit my sister?

170
00:10:03,280 --> 00:10:06,280
If you're looking to get killed, then go right ahead.

171
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:19,280
We're here! The sunset looks lovely from this hill. I highly recommend this spot for date nights, by the way.

172
00:10:19,280 --> 00:10:20,280
Uh...

173
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:23,280
I'll have some nummies ready for you when you get back!

174
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:25,280
Okay. Get it done, you three.

175
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:26,280
Thanks!

176
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:27,280
Bye!

177
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:32,280
Well, let's go! This way!

178
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:41,280
Couldn't he have just taken us right to the entrance of the dungeon?

179
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:42,280
Nope. Sorry.

180
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:45,280
Jinro can only send people places he's already been.

181
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:51,280
It looks like he dropped us off pretty close!

182
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:09,280
Right, let's do this!

183
00:11:09,280 --> 00:11:12,280
Who asked you to tag along anyway?

184
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:19,280
I still don't understand how the Wizard King even knows about Asta.

185
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:21,280
And you probably never will.

186
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:31,280
Fact is, Wizard King sees things we don't. Also, he's weird.

187
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:32,280
Huh?

188
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:37,280
It's so dark in here.

189
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:41,280
Could you maybe stop clinging like that? I can barely walk over here.

190
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:43,280
Excuse me? I do not cling!

191
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:45,280
Whoa!

192
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:49,280
I can't see anything!

193
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,280
Oh, oh, oh!

194
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:57,280
Thank you! I love having my foot stopped!

195
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:59,280
What do you want from me? It's pitch black here!

196
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:01,280
Calm down, would you?

197
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:05,280
Well, maybe I would be calmer if you hadn't broken our only lantern!

198
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:06,280
You klutz!

199
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:09,280
I only broke it because you tripped and ran into me!

200
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:10,280
I am royalty!

201
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:12,280
Royals don't trip!

202
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:13,280
Clearly they do!

203
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:14,280
Insect!

204
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:16,280
Is this it?

205
00:12:16,280 --> 00:12:17,280
Let's see...

206
00:12:17,280 --> 00:12:18,280
Oh, it's bright!

207
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:19,280
I'm afraid!

208
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:49,260
Oh, my God.

209
00:12:49,280 --> 00:13:11,160
Whoa! This is like the most awesome place ever! It's so sparkly! So cool!

210
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:15,180
What's going on in here?

211
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:17,860
It looks like the space has been warped because of all the magic!

212
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:23,040
There's way more than I detected outside! The air is crazy thick!

213
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:27,500
Yes. I don't think I've ever been somewhere so steeped in mana.

214
00:13:28,740 --> 00:13:29,820
How can you tell?

215
00:13:30,700 --> 00:13:34,180
Wait, you're standing in a room full of this much mana and you can't feel it?

216
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:35,220
No, nothing.

217
00:13:35,780 --> 00:13:40,180
Well, I suppose that does make sense. Amazing how different people without magic are.

218
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:41,440
You don't have to rub it in!

219
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:46,040
It's not fair! I want to be able to feel mana too!

220
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,840
No! I want my own mana!

221
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:52,540
Do you know how lucky you royals are? You all seem to have boatloads of it!

222
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:56,440
The source of all magic power and I don't have a single drop!

223
00:13:56,660 --> 00:13:59,120
I'm empty! Just a hollow shell!

224
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:05,960
Oh! Why? Why me? What's that?

225
00:14:08,540 --> 00:14:10,680
Whoa! Is that trap magic?

226
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:23,660
Try to be more careful! You almost got us all killed!

227
00:14:24,020 --> 00:14:25,280
My bad, sorry!

228
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:29,660
Hey! Take a look at this, Asta! Right there!

229
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:31,600
I don't see anything.

230
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:33,260
Closer!

231
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:42,900
What'd you do that for?

232
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:45,300
That was so much fun to watch!

233
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,260
What are you playing at?

234
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:49,360
Oh! Another one!

235
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:49,860
Mm-hmm!

236
00:14:55,740 --> 00:14:56,360
Yeah!

237
00:14:56,360 --> 00:15:03,500
Heads up!

238
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:08,680
Coming in!

239
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:15,200
Wow! You guys should see the looks on your faces!

240
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:17,840
That was fun, huh?

241
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:20,240
I could play in this place all day!

242
00:15:22,140 --> 00:15:24,700
This guy is totally going to get us killed!

243
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:27,080
Dungeons are no joke.

244
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:28,960
I wonder how those two are doing.

245
00:15:29,580 --> 00:15:32,460
They know they're out on a mission that's both important and dangerous.

246
00:15:32,780 --> 00:15:35,280
They'll give them a chance to push their limits and grow.

247
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:36,280
Probably.

248
00:15:36,980 --> 00:15:37,420
Probably.

249
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:40,000
No, don't worry about it.

250
00:15:40,020 --> 00:15:40,900
They're going to be fine.

251
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:41,700
Luck's with them.

252
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:45,160
Ain't no one out there who can sense mana better than him.

253
00:15:45,940 --> 00:15:47,400
That includes the royals.

254
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:50,120
All the squads would have been after them.

255
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:52,520
Not for that defective personality of his.

256
00:15:54,700 --> 00:15:57,620
It's his busted personality that's got me worried.

257
00:15:58,180 --> 00:15:59,300
I'll turn to that.

258
00:16:01,540 --> 00:16:02,500
Oh, man.

259
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:05,660
Your anti-magic sword is seriously something else, Asta.

260
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:09,640
Maybe that's why the Wizard King specifically asked for you.

261
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:12,900
I'm looking forward to taking you on in a couple years.

262
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:17,680
All you have to do is make sure that sword of yours is at the ready and we should have it made.

263
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:19,700
This dungeon will be a piece of cake.

264
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:20,420
